card.statement:
We call $M$ an $AW_\mu$-module if it is a module for both the solenoidal Lie algebra $W_\mu$ and the commutative unital algebra $A = \C [t_1^{\pm 1}, \ldots, t_n^{\pm 1}]$ with these two structures being compatible:

\begin{equation}
x (f v) = (x f) v + f (x v), \quad f \in A, \; x \in W_\mu, \; v \in M.
\end{equation}
